      "text": "Let's denote the four positive integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). According to the problem, when these integers are divided by 11, they leave remainders of 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11},\\]\n\\[d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}.\\]\nWe need to find the remainder when the sum of these four integers, \\(a + b + c + d\\), is divided by 11. Using the properties of congruences, we can add the congruences together:\n\\[a + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}.\\]\nNow, we calculate the sum on the right-hand side:\n\\[2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20.\\]\nSo, we have:\n\\[a + b + c + d \\equiv 20 \\pmod{11}.\\]\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. We perform the division:\n\\[20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9.\\]\nThis means:\n\\[20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}.\\]\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by 11 is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
