      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let the four integers be $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$. We are given that $a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}$, $b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}$, $c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}$, and $d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}$. We want to find the remainder when $a + b + c + d$ is divided by $11$.\n\nWe can use the properties of congruences to simplify the expression. First, let's add the congruences together:\n\n\\[\na + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to calculate $2 + 4 + 6 + 8$:\n\n\\[\n2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$:\n\n\\[\n20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when $a + b + c + d$ is divided by $11$ is $\\boxed{9}$.",
