      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given four positive integers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) that, when divided by 11, leave remainders of 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively, we can express these integers as:\n\\[ a = 11k_1 + 2 \\]\n\\[ b = 11k_2 + 4 \\]\n\\[ c = 11k_3 + 6 \\]\n\\[ d = 11k_4 + 8 \\]\nfor some integers \\(k_1\\), \\(k_2\\), \\(k_3\\), and \\(k_4\\).\n\nThe sum of these integers is:\n\\[ a + b + c + d = (11k_1 + 2) + (11k_2 + 4) + (11k_3 + 6) + (11k_4 + 8) \\]\n\\[ = 11(k_1 + k_2 + k_3 + k_4) + 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\]\n\\[ = 11(k_1 + k_2 + k_3 + k_4) + 20 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11. Since \\(11(k_1 + k_2 + k_3 + k_4)\\) is divisible by 11, it contributes 0 to the remainder when divided by 11. Therefore, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is the same as the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. \n\nCalculating the remainder of 20 when divided by 11:\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9 \\]\n\nSo, the remainder when \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]",
